      <div class="eyebrow">THE MAUI ATLAS</div>
      <h1>Best Beach in Maui for Family Pictures (With Real Examples)</h1>
      <p class="atlas-deck">Not all beaches are created equal for portraits. Here is an honest, side-by-side comparison of Mokapu, Maluaka, and Kanaha to help you choose the ideal location for your family session.</p>
      <p class="atlas-byline">BY LAURENCE BALTER · FOUNDER &amp; LEAD PHOTOGRAPHER, WAILEA PHOTO</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OPENING NOTE -->
  <section class="atlas-opening-note" aria-label="Maui Atlas field note">
    <span>LOCATION SELECTION</span>
    <p>Matching your family’s energy, kids' ages, and lighting preferences with the right beach ensures a relaxed and stunning portrait experience.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- BEACH 1: MOKAPU BEACH (IMAGE LEFT / CONTENT RIGHT) -->
  <section class="content-split">
    <div class="content-split-image reveal visible">
      <img src="assets/wailea-photo-mokapu-sunset.jpg" width="1442" height="960" alt="Family sunset photo session at Mokapu Beach in Wailea" loading="lazy">
      <div class="atlas-photo-caption">Mokapu Beach at Sunset · Wailea</div>
    </div>
    <div class="content-split-copy reveal visible">
      <div class="chapter">SOUTH MAUI · WAILEA</div>
      <h2>Mokapu Beach: The Golden Standard for Sunset</h2>
      <p>Framed by lava rock points, soft golden sand, and views of Molokini, Mokapu Beach in Wailea offers classic resort-style elegance with gentle tide conditions.</p>

      <div class="beach-specs">
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Morning vs. Sunset Light</span>
          <p><strong>Sunset Champion:</strong> Offers ideal horizon views for golden hour glow and rich twilight colors. Morning light is bright and crisp.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Wind Conditions</span>
          <p>Protected by surrounding resort structures; wind remains light to moderate most afternoons.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Parking &amp; Privacy</span>
          <p>Dedicated public lot at Ulua/Mokapu. Moderate foot traffic near resorts, but spacious enough for private angles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Water Color &amp; Toddler Suitability</span>
          <p>Turquoise-blue hues year-round. Smooth shore entry and calm shorebreak make it exceptional for toddlers and young children.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BEACH 2: MALUAKA BEACH (CONTENT LEFT / IMAGE RIGHT) -->
  <section class="content-split reverse">
    <div class="content-split-image reveal visible">
      <img src="assets/Maluaka-Beach-at-sunset.jpg" width="1442" height="960" alt="Sunset portrait at Maluaka Beach in Makena" loading="lazy">
      <div class="atlas-photo-caption">Maluaka Beach at Sunset · Makena</div>
    </div>
    <div class="content-split-copy reveal visible">
      <div class="chapter">SOUTH MAUI · MAKENA</div>
      <h2>Maluaka Beach: Spacious Sands &amp; Lush Tropics</h2>
      <p>Tucked further south in Makena, Maluaka features expansive golden sand, kiawe foliage, and dramatic views of Kahoolawe and Haleakala's western slope.</p>

      <div class="beach-specs">
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Morning vs. Sunset Light</span>
          <p><strong>Versatile Both:</strong> Soft morning light against green backdrop; dramatic, open-sky sunset exposures with warm gradients.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Wind Conditions</span>
          <p>Extremely sheltered. Frequently enjoys the calmest breeze in South Maui during late afternoon hours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Parking &amp; Privacy</span>
          <p>Paved parking lot with restrooms. Less crowded than central Wailea beaches, providing a peaceful experience.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Water Color &amp; Toddler Suitability</span>
          <p>Deep aqua-blue water. Wide sand deck gives kids room to run, though shorebreak can pick up slightly in winter swells.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BEACH 3: KANAHA BEACH (IMAGE LEFT / CONTENT RIGHT) -->
  <section class="content-split">
    <div class="content-split-image reveal visible">
      <img src="assets/Kanaha-Beach-Turquoise-Water.jpg" width="1442" height="960" alt="Crystal clear turquoise water at Kanaha Beach Park in Kahului" loading="lazy">
      <div class="atlas-photo-caption">Kanaha Beach Turquoise Water · Kahului</div>
    </div>
    <div class="content-split-copy reveal visible">
      <div class="chapter">NORTH SHORE · KAHULUI</div>
      <h2>Kanaha Beach: Vibrant Waters &amp; Morning Quiet</h2>
      <p>A North Shore gem featuring uncrowded stretches of sand, emerald-turquoise water, views of the West Maui Mountains, and iconic coconut palms.</p>

      <div class="beach-specs">
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Morning vs. Sunset Light</span>
          <p><strong>Morning Specialty:</strong> Unbeatable early morning light with vivid blue-water saturation. Sunsets are calm but soft behind mountains.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Wind Conditions</span>
          <p>Calm early morning (7–9 AM). Trade winds pick up noticeably after 11 AM, making morning sessions essential.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Parking &amp; Privacy</span>
          <p>Abundant shade and parking lots. High morning privacy with long, quiet stretches away from resort crowds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <span class="label">Water Color &amp; Toddler Suitability</span>
          <p>Striking, clear turquoise lagoon protected by outer reef. Shallow shorelines make it perfect for young explorers in the morning.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

